---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Technical | IKTVA 2027">
  <section class="tech-page">
    <div class="container">
      <h1 class="page-title animate-in" style="--delay: 0.1s">Technical</h1>
      <p class="page-desc animate-in" style="--delay: 0.2s">Screen specifications, forced perspective workflow, and rendering pipeline documentation.</p>

      <div class="doc-sections">
        <article class="doc-section animate-in" style="--delay: 0.3s">
          <h2 class="section-label">Forced Perspective / Anamorphic 3D</h2>
          <div class="doc-content">
            <p>The event film uses forced-perspective projection across curved multi-panel screens. Viewed from a designated sweet spot in the audience, flat 2D content appears to extend into three-dimensional space.</p>
            <h3>Key concepts</h3>
            <ul>
              <li><strong>Sweet spot</strong>: the audience position where the 3D illusion is strongest. Needs to be plotted from venue dimensions and screen geometry.</li>
              <li><strong>UV pass / screen format</strong>: a flat export that looks distorted but corrects when projected onto the curved screen and viewed from the sweet spot. Similar to Ocean Outdoor's DeepScreen workflow for Piccadilly Lights.</li>
              <li><strong>VR validation</strong>: test forced perspective in VR before the event to verify the illusion works at the correct viewing angle.</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>Reference</h3>
            <ul>
              <li><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-fpobu4hv0o" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">MasterChef curved-screen setup (YouTube)</a> - at 0:45, shows the distorted flat export that corrects on screen</li>
              <li><a href="https://blenderartists.org/t/how-to-render-3d-anamorphic-movie-on-curved-screen-or-fake-3d-image/1300925/3" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Blender Artists: anamorphic rendering on curved screens</a></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="doc-section animate-in" style="--delay: 0.4s">
          <h2 class="section-label">Screen Setup</h2>
          <div class="doc-content">
            <p>Dharan Expo, Hall 1. Screen dimensions are based on previous IKTVA screen specs (exact specs TBC from staging team). Screen length is adjustable.</p>
            <h3>What we need from the staging team</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Final screen panel dimensions and curvature radius</li>
              <li>Screen resolution per panel</li>
              <li>Projector positions and throw distances</li>
              <li>Audience seating layout (for sweet-spot calculation)</li>
              <li>Media server specs and accepted delivery formats</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>Laser integration</h3>
            <p>External laser supplier recommended over Saudi-based options. Kit import under the local entity is the preferred route. Being coordinated with Soul TPHQ.</p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="doc-section animate-in" style="--delay: 0.5s">
          <h2 class="section-label">Rendering Pipeline</h2>
          <div class="doc-content">
            <p>Animation built in Cinema 4D. The rendering pipeline needs to output both standard preview renders and the UV-mapped screen format for the final delivery.</p>
            <h3>Pipeline steps</h3>
            <ol>
              <li>Model the event space at scale (Hall 1 mock-up)</li>
              <li>Animate content in standard camera view</li>
              <li>Apply UV pass to remap animation onto the screen geometry</li>
              <li>Export distorted flat video for each screen panel</li>
              <li>Test in VR or on-site with projection</li>
            </ol>
            <h3>File naming</h3>
            <p>TBC. Establish a convention before the team starts producing final renders.</p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="doc-section animate-in" style="--delay: 0.6s">
          <h2 class="section-label">Code and Scripts</h2>
          <div class="doc-content">
            <p>Reusable scripts and tools live in the <code>scripts/</code> directory of this repo. Add Cinema 4D scripts, Python utilities, and render automation here.</p>
            <p class="hint">To add a script: commit it to the <code>scripts/</code> folder and document its purpose in a comment at the top of the file.</p>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .tech-page {
    min-height: 100vh;
    padding-top: calc(var(--header-height) + var(--space-xl));
  }

  .page-title {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
  }

  .page-desc {
    color: var(--color-fg-muted);
    margin-top: var(--space-xs);
    max-width: 600px;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .doc-sections {
    margin-top: var(--space-lg);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .section-label {
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.15em;
    color: var(--color-fg-muted);
    font-weight: 600;
    padding-bottom: var(--space-xs);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .doc-content {
    margin-top: var(--space-sm);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    max-width: 680px;
  }

  .doc-content p {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .doc-content h3 {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-top: var(--space-md);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xs);
  }

  .doc-content ul, .doc-content ol {
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .doc-content li {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .doc-content a {
    color: var(--color-accent);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
  }

  .doc-content code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    background: var(--color-bg-muted);
    padding: 0.125rem 0.375rem;
    border-radius: 3px;
  }

  .hint {
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--color-fg-muted);
    padding: var(--space-sm);
    background: var(--color-bg-muted);
    border-radius: 4px;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--color-accent);
  }
</style>
